                <person xml:id="BAN06" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Saxe</forename>
                        <surname>Bannister</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1790">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1877"/>
                    <occupation>Lawyer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Son of John Bannister (q.v.) the actor. Godwin knew him after his stint
                            as Attorney General in Australia. He seems likely to have been
                            introduced by his father, who had retired in 1815 and died in 1836. The
                            first entry seems to be an occasion on which Bannister calls on Godwin.
                            The contacts between S Bannister and Godwin are wholly around the time
                            of the campaign for and then the passing of the Reform Act of 1832.</p>
                    </note>
